From: Blakestream-GaintB V2.2
Subject: [PATCH] api: remove arbitrary-path save command

sgminer runs as root on the controller and its loopback API is reachable by
local processes. The legacy save command accepts an arbitrary pathname and
writes the current configuration there, turning any local web-process
compromise into a root file-clobber primitive. The dashboard persists its
configuration through dedicated validated helpers and does not need this API
verb, so omit it from the dispatch table entirely.

The implementation can remain for upstream compatibility, but no API group
can resolve or invoke it after this change.

---
--- a/api.c
+++ b/api.c
@@ -3725,7 +3725,6 @@ struct CMDS {
     {"gpuengine",          gpuengine,      true, false},
     {"gpufan",             gpufan,         true, false},
     {"gpuvddc",            gpuvddc,        true, false},
-    {"save",   dosave,   true, false},
     {"quit",   doquit,   true, false},
     {"privileged",   privileged, true, false},
     {"notify",   notify,   false,  true},
